S=[]
S.append(("Huntsville at a glance","""<p>Huntsville has 233,627 residents and is Alabama's biggest city. It serves as seat of Madison County, but the city boundary spills into Limestone, Morgan and Marshall counties as well. A Huntsville mailing address therefore does not guarantee which county sends your tax bill. Look up the parcel first. Madison County's collector bills only the land inside Madison County.</p><p>Aerospace and defense employment feeds local housing demand, with NASA's Marshall center and Cummings Research Park among the anchors. Families transferred for a contract or a plant job frequently need to close fast, and a seller who can pick a closing date to suit the buyer has an edge.</p><p>Homes range from Old Town houses dating to the late 1820s to the ranches and split levels that spread outward after Redstone Arsenal turned into a rocket research center. Plenty of the postwar houses are due for new roofs, wiring and plumbing. Inside a historic district, design review rules can apply, so phone the city before any exterior project or demolition.</p>"""))
S.append(("Due dates and payment options","""<p>For the Madison County portion of Huntsville, the tax collector sends the bills and takes the payments. October 1 is the due date, and a bill is late once December 31 passes. Each bill covers a twelve-month span that begins the prior October 1.</p><p>State law does not oblige the county to mail a bill before the delinquency date. A courtesy notice goes out by October 1 and a final notice follows after January 1, yet a missing envelope is no defense. Ring 256-532-3370 or search the parcel online if yours never shows up.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Payment method</th><th>Cost or limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Card or debit</td><td>2.75 percent convenience fee plus $0.30</td></tr><tr><td>E-check</td><td>$1.50</td></tr><tr><td>Real property in April and May</td><td>Certified funds, cash or cards only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Walk-in service is at the Madison County Service Center, 1918 Memorial Parkway NW, Monday through Friday from 8:30 a.m. until 4:30 p.m. There is also a satellite counter at 100 Plaza Blvd. in the town of Madison.</p>"""))
S.append(("Tax rate and how the bill is built","""<p>Inside Huntsville city limits the county's posted figure is $5.80 per $100 of assessed value. Nearby posted figures include $6.95 for Madison, $6.15 for Triana and $4.05 for New Hope, Gurley and Owens Cross Roads. Unincorporated land shows $3.35 and improvements $3.65.</p><p>Appraised value is multiplied by a class percentage to get assessed value. Utilities fall at 30 percent and general property at 20 percent. Farmland, timber and a single-family home you live in are taxed at 10 percent. On the standard homestead worksheet, $48 comes off when assessed value reaches $4,000 or more.</p><p>What you owe depends on your own appraisal and exemptions, and only the parcel record shows both.</p>"""))
S.append(("What happens if the tax goes unpaid?","""<p>Once December 31 passes, a $5.00 late fee attaches and interest builds at 1 percent monthly on the base tax. Probate and advertising charges pile on top.</p><p>Delinquency begins January 1 under the state schedule. Probate court receives the file in February, hears matters in March, and notices are advertised in April. The sale comes in May, and Madison County runs its yearly lien auction online.</p><p>Settling the account ahead of the auction is much cheaper than redeeming afterward. When back taxes are what is pushing you to sell, say so up front so the title company can put the exact payoff on the closing statement.</p>"""))
S.append(("How to appeal your assessment","""<p>A written protest goes to the Madison County Board of Equalization, upstairs in the Service Center at 1918 Memorial Parkway NW. The legal basis is Code of Alabama sections 40-3-20, 40-3-24 and 40-3-25.</p><ul><li>Notice of new values usually appears in March or April as a newspaper ad that runs two weeks in succession.</li><li>The 30-day window to protest starts with the second ad.</li><li>An appraiser looks at your case first; a hearing is scheduled only if the two of you still differ.</li><li>Going on to circuit court means filing within 30 days after the board adjourns, with the tax paid by December 31 or a bond for twice the tax posted.</li></ul><p>Bring photos of damage, repair estimates and recent sales of similar houses close by. An appraiser can weigh those.</p>"""))
S.append(("What happens to the tax bill when you sell?","""<p>Tax is billed to whoever owned the parcel on October 1 of the prior year, which means a buyer may get a notice addressed to you. A new owner should check that the deed is on file with the probate office in the Service Center, then register the property with the Tax Assessor's Office and claim any exemptions.</p><p>Title companies usually split the year's tax between the two sides at closing. Request the proration worksheet and hold on to the paid receipt. Where tax remains unpaid, the closer asks the collector for a payoff number and deducts it from what you receive.</p><p>Before listing, gather your last paid tax receipt, the parcel number and the deed details. If you are not sure the deed is recorded, ask the probate office to confirm. Clearing that up early keeps a buyer's title search from turning up surprises in the final days before closing.</p>"""))
S.append(("Ground and weather problems that surface at sale","""<p>Severe weather is the chief hazard. Spring and late fall storms bring big hail, damaging wind and tornadoes, and Huntsville lies in Dixie Alley, known for long-track twisters. Damaged roofs and siding come up quickly with buyers who need a mortgage or homeowner's insurance.</p><p>The ground is karst, with caves threading the limestone below. Sinkholes and odd drainage are possible. Cracks from settling, doors that stick or a soft patch in the yard tend to get flagged by an inspector working for a retail buyer.</p><p>A cash buyer willing to take the house as is sidesteps the haggling.</p>"""))
S.append(("Common situations for Huntsville sellers","""<ul><li>Inherited houses where several heirs share title and no one is the clear owner of record.</li><li>Older mill-village and Old Town houses that need major systems work.</li><li>Hail-damaged roofs from spring storms.</li><li>Job moves tied to Redstone Arsenal, Cummings Research Park or the auto plants.</li><li>Delinquent tax on a rental or vacant house.</li></ul><p>A buyer who closes when you want and accepts the house in its present state helps in every case above. Cash Home Buyers writes offers on Huntsville houses and uses a local title company to pay off delinquent tax out of the proceeds. Skipping the lender appraisal, repair requests and financing contingency removes the usual points where a sale falls apart.</p>"""))
F=[("What is the Huntsville property tax rate?","Inside city limits, Madison County posts $5.80 per $100 of assessed value. Parcels in the Limestone, Morgan or Marshall slices of Huntsville are billed by those counties instead, so confirm which one applies."),
("When is Huntsville property tax due?","The due date is October 1, and delinquency starts after December 31. A courtesy notice is mailed by October 1, though the county is not obliged to send one."),
("Where do I pay property tax in Huntsville?","Pay in person at the Service Center, 1918 Memorial Parkway NW, or at the satellite counter, 100 Plaza Blvd. in Madison. Online and mail payments work too. The main phone line is 256-532-3370."),
("What is the penalty for late property tax in Huntsville?","After December 31 there is a $5.00 fee, interest of 1 percent monthly on the base tax, and probate and advertising costs. Parcels still unpaid can be offered at the May online lien sale."),
("Can I sell a Huntsville house that owes back taxes?","Yes. The balance is paid out of your proceeds at closing, using a payoff amount the title company gets from the collector.")]
w('huntsville-al-property-tax-guide',S,F)
